       The _a_t_t_r___s_e_t and _a_t_t_r___c_l_r members are used to specify the mount proper‐
       ties  that are supposed to be set or cleared for a mount or mount tree.
       Flags set in _a_t_t_r___s_e_t enable a property on a mount or mount  tree,  and
       flags set in _a_t_t_r___c_l_r remove a property from a mount or mount tree.

       When  changing  mount properties, the kernel will first clear the flags
       specified in the _a_t_t_r___c_l_r field, and then set the  flags  specified  in
       the _a_t_t_r___s_e_t field.  For example, these settings:

           struct mount_attr attr = {
               .attr_clr = MOUNT_ATTR_NOEXEC | MOUNT_ATTR_NODEV,
               .attr_set = MOUNT_ATTR_RDONLY | MOUNT_ATTR_NOSUID,
           };

       are equivalent to the following steps:

           unsigned int current_mnt_flags = mnt->mnt_flags;

           /*
            * Clear all flags set in .attr_clr,
            * clearing MOUNT_ATTR_NOEXEC and MOUNT_ATTR_NODEV.
            */
           current_mnt_flags &= ~attr->attr_clr;

           /*
            * Now set all flags set in .attr_set,
            * applying MOUNT_ATTR_RDONLY and MOUNT_ATTR_NOSUID.
            */
           current_mnt_flags |= attr->attr_set;

           mnt->mnt_flags = current_mnt_flags;

